      "message": "This is much more aggressive blocking behavior than the existing ashmem shrinker has - the existing one has bounded waiting for any pin/unpin calls - note the `mutex_trylock()` it uses at the end of each loop iteration - if someone else is trying to do a pin/unpin operation, and a shrink is in progress, it will only ever process one item before letting the `pin`/`unpin` proceed.",
